  "note": "Supplied input files, unchanged by the benchmark. Source-file hashes, optional provenance, decoded/file point counts, thinning factors and loaded bounds are recorded. Production hybrid WebGPU C2C, same snapshots, spatial partitions, Morton query order, reference construction and worker counts. Await the already-started automatic CPU pool warm-up before any fixture/trial; its time is recorded separately and excluded. Five unmeasured full-sort/median-selection warm-up pairs precede alternating timed pairs. Times include planning, copies/transfers, tree builds, distances, joining and exact summaries; file load/rendering are excluded. Every timed pair must match displayed f32 distance bits and exact f64 statistics. Native builds/non-SIMD WASM remain scalar. CPU clocks, power and other applications are uncontrolled; no cross-machine speed guarantee. Only median calculation differs: sortedMillis uses full total_cmp sorting, selectedMillis selects the upper middle and (for even sizes) the maximum lower-partition value. Equal nonzero extrema with a non-NaN sum skip median scratch allocation; a complete total-order scan also permits directly reading ordered inputs when endpoints match the extrema. The input reduction order and midpoint arithmetic are identical. Both CPU controls use scalar leaves and progressive joining; GPU controls use default prefetch, bounds, SIMD verification, batches and workgroups with reference/device reuse. GPU phase intervals exclude final summaries and can overlap; do not add them to infer wall time."
